  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 1248 AM CDT Sun Oct 25 2026\n\nTuesday-Thursday...The next shortwave trough rotates into the \nNorthern Plains, spawning another low pressure system across the \nDakotas. Diffluent flow ahead of a jet streak in the base of this \ntrough is expected to slowly deepen this new low as it treks into \nMinnesota and southern Ontario Tuesday night into Wednesday. A weak \ncold front will slide into Iowa, but similar to today, it will stall \nout across the state heading into Wednesday night. Lingering \nmoisture from the Pacific though keeps isolated PoPs (20-40%) \naround Wednesday into Thursday.\n\nFriday-Saturday...Another weak trough in the subtropical jet \nstream is pulled northward into the Central Plains by a longwave\ntrough digging into the western CONUS. A sense of deju vu sets \nin on Friday with surface cyclogenesis occurring along the Front\nRange of the Rockies and easterly surface flow returning with a\nhigh pressure over the Great Lakes. By Saturday, the remnants \nof the boundary left across Iowa is lifted northward, and \nsoutherly flow returns. This will set the stage for a more \nactive pattern going into the first days of November.",
